<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- The sunbeam that falls over the wielder when UMW_RallyingCry fires (AbilityDefs/RallyingCry.xml,
       spawned by the vanilla CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget on that def).

       A deliberate self-contained COPY of Core's `Lightshaft` FleckDef
       (Data/Core/Defs/Effects/Fleck_Visual.xml) — same texture, same `Lightshaft` shader and shader
       parameters, same width-pulse curve — because Core's version cannot be a `ParentName` target (it
       has no `Name=`) and, more importantly, its timings are tuned for a *permanent ambient emitter*:
       Core spawns it from EffecterDef UndercaveMapExitLightshafts (chancePerTick, maintainTicks 9999)
       on the `CaveExit` building, which is the light-shaft effect seen in Anomaly's undercave and
       Odyssey's insect lair. A 3s fade-in reads as atmosphere, not as a triggered moment.

       What changed from Core, and why:
         • fadeIn 3 -> 0.35, fadeOut 3 -> 1.5, solidTime 1 -> 4.15, life 7s -> 6.0s. The beam has to land
           *with* the cry, and its life is matched to the cast pose (0.5s warmup + 5s
           verbProperties.defaultCooldownTime = 5.5s of raised weapon) so the light outlasts the pose by
           only a beat. Settled by eye in play.
         • scaleTime 7 -> 3, i.e. HALF the lifetime, so the width pulse flares once as the beam lands and
           the beam then holds its base width for the rest. That is not a repeat: CurvedScalerExt
           .ScaleAtTime evaluates the curve at Mathf.Clamp01(ageSecs / scaleTime), so past scaleTime the
           input pins at 1 where this curve's last point is 0 — the scaler simply stops contributing and
           the x-axis scale sits back at 1. A pulse cannot loop (decompile-verified, RimWorld 1.6). Raise
           scaleTime to the full 6 if the flare should instead stretch across the whole beam's life.
         • unattachedDrawOffset (0,0,4) added. FleckStatic.Setup feeds def.unattachedDrawOffset into
           FleckDrawPosition, so this raises the shaft to put its lower end on the pawn instead of
           centring a 10-cell beam through them. 4 = 0.4 x drawSize, the same size-to-offset ratio
           Core's cave-exit sub-effecter uses (positionOffset z 8 at an effective size of 20).
         • drawSize left at Core's 10.0 and the comp's `scale` left at its default 1, i.e. half the
           on-screen size of the cave-exit spawn (which uses scale 2) — one pawn, not a cave mouth.
         • alpha on both colours .8 -> 1. The `Lightshaft` shader is Core's own and exposes only
           _dayColor, _nightColor and _DustTex1 — there is no brightness multiplier to reach for — so the
           fourth component is the whole intensity knob, and Core's .8 is set for an ambient cave-mouth
           shaft rather than a triggered moment. The hue is left exactly as Core's, day and night.
           IF STILL TOO FAINT, in escalating order: push the RGB toward white (this washes out the warm
           day / cold night contrast, so it costs something), or list UMW_RallyingCryLightshaft TWICE in
           the ability's CompProperties_AbilityFleckOnTarget fleckDefs, which spawns two coincident
           beams that compound. Neither is needed yet.
       drawSize/offset/timings are the eyeball-tunable knobs here, and still want an in-game visual
       check. Rotation is deliberately 0 (Core tilts its ambient shafts 15 degrees): light straight
       down over the wielder. -->
  <FleckDef ParentName="FleckBase">
    <defName>UMW_RallyingCryLightshaft</defName>
    <altitudeLayer>MoteOverhead</altitudeLayer>
    <fadeInTime>0.35</fadeInTime>
    <solidTime>4.15</solidTime>
    <fadeOutTime>1.5</fadeOutTime>
    <unattachedDrawOffset>(0, 0, 4)</unattachedDrawOffset>
    <graphicData>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_FleckPulse</graphicClass>
      <texPath>Things/Mote/Lightshaft</texPath>
      <shaderType>Lightshaft</shaderType>
      <renderQueue>4000</renderQueue>
      <shaderParameters>
        <_dayColor>(1, .73, .56, 1)</_dayColor>
        <_nightColor>(.37, .8, .89, 1)</_nightColor>
        <_DustTex1>/Things/Mote/LightshaftNoise</_DustTex1>
      </shaderParameters>
      <drawSize>10.0</drawSize>
    </graphicData>
    <scalers>
      <li>
        <scaleAmt>.2~1</scaleAmt>
        <scaleTime>3</scaleTime> <!-- half the 6s life: flare once on landing, then hold base width -->
        <axisMask>(1, 0, 0)</axisMask>
        <curve>
          <points>
            <li>(0,0)</li>
            <li>(0.04,0.1647907)</li>
            <li>(0.08,0.3134471)</li>
            <li>(0.12,0.4462824)</li>
            <li>(0.16,0.5636099)</li>
            <li>(0.2,0.6657428)</li>
            <li>(0.24,0.7529945)</li>
            <li>(0.28,0.8256782)</li>
            <li>(0.32,0.8841072)</li>
            <li>(0.36,0.9285948)</li>
            <li>(0.3999999,0.9594542)</li>
            <li>(0.4399999,0.9769989)</li>
            <li>(0.4799999,0.981542)</li>
            <li>(0.5199999,0.9733967)</li>
            <li>(0.5599999,0.9528764)</li>
            <li>(0.6,0.9202945)</li>
            <li>(0.64,0.875964)</li>
            <li>(0.68,0.8201982)</li>
            <li>(0.72,0.7533107)</li>
            <li>(0.7600001,0.6756145)</li>
            <li>(0.8000001,0.587423)</li>
            <li>(0.8400001,0.4890493)</li>
            <li>(0.8800001,0.3808068)</li>
            <li>(0.9200001,0.2630088)</li>
            <li>(0.9600002,0.1359687)</li>
            <li>(1,0)</li>
          </points>
        </curve>
      </li>
    </scalers>
  </FleckDef>

</Defs>
